<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.weeklyrollup</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py</string>
        <string>--weekly-rollup</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Runs once a week, Sunday 6:00pm -- ahead of the new work week,
         a longer-form summary on top of the twice-daily briefing
         everyone gets. Grace-exclusive (curant-cli's weekly_rollup()
         checks the tier); safe to load on every Mac regardless of
         tier, same "safe to always run" pattern as the other scheduled
         jobs. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>18</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-weeklyrollup.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-weeklyrollup-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp com.curant.weeklyrollup.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.weeklyrollup.plist

Grace-exclusive, gated in curant-cli's weekly_rollup() function (checks
get_customer_august_tier(config) == "grace") -- loading this job on a
non-Grace customer's Mac is harmless, it just always results in
should_send=false, same "safe to always run" pattern as the other
scheduled jobs.

To test immediately rather than waiting for Sunday evening, run
curant-watcher.py with the --weekly-rollup flag directly (see
ProgramArguments above).

Logs land at /tmp/curant-weeklyrollup.log and /tmp/curant-weeklyrollup-error.log.
-->
